Coefficient generator workspaces and recipes

smash_equilibrium/  generate_vh_coeff_smash_equilibrium.sh  hrg_eos=4
smash_pce_light/    generate_vh_coeff_smash_pce_light.sh    hrg_eos=5
smash/             generate_vh_coeff_smash.sh              legacy hrg_eos=2
smash_box/         generate_vh_coeff_smash_box.sh          hrg_eos=3
urqmd/             generate_vh_coeff_urqmd.sh              hrg_eos=1

Recipes are invoked from this directory. Each copies the selected particle list
to its workspace as pdg.dat, builds the table generator, and copies its output
to ../deltaf_coefficients/vh/. The pdg_smash_pce.dat particle list
keeps sigma excluded. The box-format particle parser is also
used for this PCE list; it is a file format, not the coefficient table name.

WARNING(PCE): legacy_pce_generator/ and its recipe
 generate_vh_coeff_legacy_pce.sh
still contain the copied single-occupancy implementation with meson/baryon
powers. The recipe writes legacy_pce_generator output, not the production
smash_pce_light_strange directory. This generator needs a physics adaptation
before it can replace the copied production two-flavor tables (hrg_eos=6).

Copied build caches and binaries retain their original paths and are historical
artifacts. The maintained sampler is built separately from ../src/cpp. Naming
changes here do not establish consistency of archived generators with the
current valence-dependent sampler; see ../README.md before regeneration.
